# The build context is transferred to the Docker daemon on every build, and COPY . . lands in the
# image. Without this, 244 MB of node_modules built for Windows is copied over the Linux ones npm ci
# just installed. It happens to work - Docker merges directories, so the linux rollup and esbuild
# binaries survive and the win32 ones are simply never loaded - but it is luck, not design, and it
# costs about two and a half minutes of context transfer per build.
node_modules
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vite reads .env.local for every mode. The Dockerfile passes the real values as build args, and
# process.env wins over the files, so the bundle is currently correct - but shipping a file that
# points at localhost:8180 into the image that builds the production bundle is a trap left armed.
.env
.env.*

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.log
.DS_Store
